# DEV instance. Caddy runs natively on the box (apt package, its own
# systemd unit). It auto-issues + renews a Let's Encrypt cert and
# reverse-proxies to the server on localhost (transparent WebSocket
# upgrade, so wss:// rides through). Install at /etc/caddy/Caddyfile.
#
# Hostname is a placeholder — confirm/change. Whatever it is, the dev
# SSM tree's GOOGLE_CALLBACK_URL must match it.
#
# mud.panterasbox.com is the CANONICAL public host (CLIENT_URL +
# GOOGLE_CALLBACK_URL in the dev SSM tree both point at it).
# dev.saxonberg.panterasbox.net is a legacy alias that still resolves
# here and gets its own auto-issued cert (listing both names in one site
# block does that), but because the app advertises the mud callback,
# login initiated on the .net alias lands back on mud.panterasbox.com.
mud.panterasbox.com, dev.saxonberg.panterasbox.net {
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy localhost:2010
}
